body: |-
  ## Conductor Revival — Phased Build Plan
  (Plan to build. Linked understand-phase: L-2026-06-15-ascend-214832-001. Feasibility GREEN.)

  ### Thesis
  Conductor = hybrid macOS desktop app: custom conversation UI over Claude Code's structured headless stream (`claude -p --output-format stream-json --input-format stream-json`), native control actions preserved, container for the presence/page/reply on-call contract. Voice = a-aloud as a swappable client.

  ### Phase 0 — Keystone spike (smallest validating step)
  PROVE: spawn one `claude -p` with stream-json in+out from Swift; render the conversation (assistant deltas, tool_use, tool_result) in a minimal custom SwiftUI view; complete one full round-trip incl. a follow-up turn over stdin. Surfaces the real gotchas (stdout buffering/ordering, process lifecycle, cleanup) on the actual target. Gate: if the stream renders cleanly and a reply lands, GO.

  ### Phase 1 — Single-session conversation surface (the friction-killer)
  Full one-session custom chat UI replacing AX terminal-scraping: streaming text, tool calls rendered live, inline permission approve/deny (route via `--permission-prompt-tool` to a Conductor MCP tool), interrupt/cancel, reply composer, per-session cwd + `--allowedTools`/`--permission-mode`. This alone removes the conversation pain for one session.

  ### Phase 2 — Fleet spine (kills terminal-window sprawl)
  N concurrent sessions: session-spine sidebar (row per CC session, grouped by project/archetype, folders/pin/archive), single-active-center, background sessions keep running. Run-supervision abstraction with PARALLEL sessions (lift Odysseus's Semaphore(1)); replay-buffer + disk-backed status (survive window close / app restart); spawn/attach/detach + `--session-id`/`--resume`.

  ### Phase 3 — Background-run + page-back (on-call contract)
  Backgrounded session completes/blocks/asks → pages you: add UserNotifications.framework (Conductor has only in-app banners today), row badge, jump-to. Wire to the settled presence/page/reply contract + soft-blocks (paradigm_propose_block) + Symphony as transport. Presence model (at_keyboard/afk/dnd/offline) gates pages. a-aloud voice = client of the same page/reply bus.

  ### Phase 4 — Hybrid web-pane integration + fleet monitor
  WKWebView host + JS↔Swift bridge protocol (Arky designs); reuse platform-ui section panes (Tasks/Lore/Graph/Team) inside Conductor rather than native-rebuilding them; fleet monitor grid fed by captain_board + ambient_health + .paradigm/remediations. Native control plane wraps web content. Honors web-primary.

  ### Phase 5 — Learning loop + identity
  Route ALL run outcomes, page/reply traces, human-interventions to ~/.paradigm/ event substrate (TaskRun-shape schema → events/*.jsonl, decision store, notebooks, calibration table). Fleet identity by archetype×project (run = live leaf). Human-intervention-on-stuck-session = teacher-escalation → distilled calibration signal. Infra-death-vs-agent-failure hygiene so calibration isn't poisoned.

  ### Cross-cutting constraints
  - Do NOT native-rebuild web Platform sections (Phase 4 reuses them).
  - ALL signals → ~/.paradigm/ substrate, never a Conductor-local store (Odysseus's scattered-store fragmentation is the cautionary tale).
  - Codesign + notarize for distribution (build-conductor.sh signs+hardens but doesn't notarize/staple yet).
  - Symphony = transport for send-to/broadcast/agent-reply.
  - Scale gotchas to design for: token quota, per-process stdout buffering, zombie cleanup on crash, background-bash killed ~5s post-session.

  ### Open design decisions owned by planning/Arky
  native↔web bridge protocol; run abstraction (process-per-session confirmed) + parallel supervision model; exact page-trigger set (soft-blocks only vs + liveness/idle + Symphony direct); spine default grouping (project vs archetype×project — inherit Tasks-section swim-lane grammar).
